	micimmptl«*
	micimmptl1.1.0"≤*Make it Compatible: Immersive Portals bundles small, self-contained compatibility patches for
Immersive Portals (NeoForge). Each patch activates only when the mods it bridges are installed, so it is safe to
keep loaded with any subset of them.

Patches in this build:
- Immersive Portals chunk stability: keeps terrain on the far side of portals from unloading at random. Stock
  Immersive Portals shrinks its portal chunk loaders whenever the client reports modest fps or low free heap
  (chronic in a large modpack) and cuts the unload grace of watched chunks when a player watches many - so
  far-side chunks visibly unloaded and re-sent in a loop. Loading ranges now stay at their full values (the
  indirectLoadingRadiusCap config remains the bound) and the unload grace stays at its normal length.
- Immersive Portals x Sable: makes portals and Sable vehicles coexist - resolves their hard collision mixin
  conflict, fixes the stock Sable+IP crash on player pose changes, keeps entities on vehicles synced and tracked,
  restores plot-chunk packet delivery (vehicle block edits reach clients), keeps vehicles loaded/visible through
  portals (cross-dimension included), keeps vehicle edits rebuilding their meshes, fixes sub-level block entities
  in portal views, and stops Immersive Portals' chunk tickets from fighting Sable's plot chunks (the "stuck on
  saving" exit hang). On top of the ported fixes, sub-levels can now travel THROUGH portals: driving a vehicle's
  pivot through a portal teleports its pose, physics body and momentum through the portal transform, carries the
  entities on deck along, and re-spaces the client's interpolation timeline so the crossing renders seamlessly
  (cross-dimension portals relocate the vehicle's plot into the destination dimension). Based on
  ImmersivePortalSableBridge by rebbyIf & Bunting_chj, adapted for Sable 2.0 and extended.
- Immersive Portals x Sodium 0.8: stock Immersive Portals 6.0.7 targets Sodium 0.6 and hard-crashes on world join
  with Sodium 0.8. This patch cancels the broken 0.6-era Sodium mixins, retires the render-list context system
  that corrupted Sodium 0.8's incremental lists (severe chunk flicker), and renders portal views stably from the
  main view's render lists - widening collection while portals are on screen so portal views stay complete.
  Dormant with Sodium 0.6 or older.
- NEO VOXY BUILD: the Voxy patch in this jar was rewritten for Neo Voxy (NHblock-Johnsnow/neo-voxy-multiversion,
  0.5.0 line) and does not apply to voxy-forged; it stays dormant if the installed Voxy does not match. It also
  keeps Voxy Server Side's LOD loading running while a cross-dimension portal is on screen. Unofficial modification
  of Make it Compatible: Immersive Portals 1.1.0 (MIT, leon.raineri); every other patch is unchanged.
- Voxy x Immersive Portals: renders Voxy's LOD terrain INSIDE portal views - each portal pass gets its own Voxy
  viewport (own frustum/occlusion/draw-list state, so neither view flickers), the portal plane is applied as a
  frustum clip, and Immersive Portals' clip-distance GL state is kept off Voxy's shaders (the old smearing).
  Cross-dimension portals show the destination's LODs when Voxy has them. Immersive Portals stays on its
  framebuffer (compatibility) renderer; known limit of that renderer (upstream): portals seen through other
  portals don't render their view.
- Immersive Portals x Simple Clouds: volumetric clouds render fully inside portal views on both portal
  renderers - portal passes stay secondary (mesh/shadow state advances only on the main pass) but draw complete
  clouds from the portal camera, with the composite retargeted into the portal framebuffer under the
  compatibility renderer (it used to smear across the screen there), per-pass fog/frustum from the portal view,
  widened cloud culling while portals are on screen, and per-pass rain/lightning. Weather is per-portal too:
  Simple Clouds keeps one smoothed storminess sampled at the player, and it drives the world fog, sky colour and
  darkening, cloud colour, cloud render distance and the storm-fog cutoff - so a portal into a storm used to stay
  bright and clear. Each portal now carries its own, sampled at the portal camera against the destination level.
  On the default (stencil) renderer, a portal into a cloudy dimension - the Overworld seen from the Nether - no
  longer turns everything around it black: Simple Clouds' compositing cleared the whole screen mid-portal.
- Immersive Portals x Better Simple Clouds: gives each portal view the in-cloud fog of its own destination.
  Better Simple Clouds tracks how thoroughly the camera is wrapped in a cloud as one value, eased towards a
  sample at the player's camera, and the in-cloud fog's distance, its cloud-coloured tint and the drifting motes
  all read it - so a portal whose far side sat inside a cloud stayed clear, and being in a cloud yourself pushed
  the whiteout into every portal view. Each portal now keeps its own, measured with Better Simple Clouds' own
  detector at the portal camera. The motes are skipped in portal views (they are world-anchored around the
  player, so they cannot follow a portal camera).

The Sable patches (LittleTiles x Sable, Sable x Iris) live in "Make it Compatible: Sable"; the Voxy patches in
"Make it Compatible: Voxy"; the Simple Clouds improvements in "Better Simple Clouds". All build from the same repo.ji
